# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fisio Architect 2.0 — environment template
# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in what you actually use.
#
# RULES (read this first):
#   1. RESOLUTION ORDER: per-role provider settings (provider, model, base
#      URL, API key) are chosen in the in-app "Providers" view and are stored
#      in your browser, then sent with each request. The values below are
#      SERVER-SIDE FALLBACKS / DEFAULTS only — they kick in when a role
#      leaves the matching field blank.
#   2. `.env` IS LOCAL-ONLY AND NEVER COMMITTED. It is gitignored; on Vercel
#      you set the same variables in Project Settings -> Environment Variables
#      (the file itself is not uploaded).
#   3. NEVER PUT SECRETS IN `VITE_*` VARIABLES. Anything prefixed `VITE_` is
#      baked into the browser bundle and visible to anyone. Only public values
#      (e.g. the Supabase anon key) belong there.
#   4. SERVER KEYS NEVER REACH THE BROWSER. The API only ever reports whether
#      a key exists (boolean), never its value.
#   You do NOT have to set every variable. Set only what your setup needs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GEMINI_API_KEY
#   Fallback key for the Gemini provider. Required only if a role uses Gemini
#   AND leaves its own API key blank in the Providers view. For local
#   `npm run dev` put your key here; on Vercel set it in the dashboard.
#   Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#   Leave blank if you are testing with Ollama (no cloud key needed at all).
GEMINI_API_KEY=""

# OPENAI_API_KEY / OPENAI_BASE_URL / OPENAI_MODEL
#   Server-side fallbacks for the "OpenAI / OpenAI-compatible" provider, used
#   only when an OpenAI role leaves the matching field blank in the Providers
#   view. Set the key here to avoid pasting it per role (and to keep it out of
#   browser localStorage). BASE_URL is handy for compatible gateways
#   (e.g. OpenRouter, a local vLLM). MODEL defaults to gpt-4o. Leave blank if
#   you configure each role in-app or don't use OpenAI.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=""
# OPENAI_BASE_URL="https://api.openai.com/v1"
# OPENAI_MODEL="gpt-4o"

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL / ANTHROPIC_MODEL
#   Same fallback pattern for the Anthropic provider. MODEL defaults to
#   claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219. Leave blank if you set keys in-app or skip Anthropic.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL="https://api.anthropic.com/v1"
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL="claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219"

# NOTE: Ollama has NO server-side variables. The Ollama base URL and model are
# configured per role in the in-app Providers view, and the browser calls your
# local Ollama directly (http://localhost:11434). See README -> "Using Ollama"
# for the one-time CORS setup (OLLAMA_ORIGINS) required on the Ollama side.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE (optional — cloud storage of articles, versions and profile rules)
#
#   Both values below are PUBLIC BY DESIGN. The browser bundle ships them to
#   whoever loads the page, which is the normal way to use Supabase: the anon
#   key grants nothing on its own because row level security decides access,
#   and the policies in supabase/schema.sql gate every row on the workspace
#   secret header.
#
#   NEVER put these here:
#     * the `service_role` key — it bypasses all policies, and anything in a
#       VITE_* variable ends up readable in the bundle;
#     * the workspace secret — it is typed once inside the app (Providers ->
#       Cloud storage) and lives in that browser's storage, not in this file
#       and not in the build, so a published bundle cannot hand it out.
#
#   Leave both blank to keep the app purely local (IndexedDB). Cloud sync stays
#   switched off until they are filled in and a workspace secret is entered.
#
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL   Project URL, shown as https://<ref>.supabase.co
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY   The "anon" public key from Project Settings ->
#                            API keys.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://REPLACE_ME.supabase.co"
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=""

# DISABLE_HMR
#   Set to "true" to turn off Vite hot-module replacement in `npm run dev`.
#   Only affects local development; ignored on Vercel.
# DISABLE_HMR="true"

# PORT
#   Port the Express server listens on. Defaults to 5177.
#   5177 is used instead of 3000 because other local dev servers commonly own
#   3000, and a stale localhost:3000 tab then shows someone else's app.
#   If the port is already in use, the server automatically tries the next one
#   and prints the URL it actually bound to.
#   Not used on Vercel (serverless functions have no port to bind).
# PORT=5177

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEPLOYING TO VERCEL
#   The file `.env` is NOT used on Vercel. In the Vercel dashboard go to
#   Project Settings -> Environment Variables and add, if you use them:
#     GEMINI_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, OPENAI_BASE_URL, OPENAI_MODEL,
#     ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, ANTHROPIC_MODEL
#     VITE_SUPABASE_URL, VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY   (read at build time — set
#     them before deploying, and they must be the PUBLIC anon key only)
#   All are optional: the app works with keys entered per role in the
#   Providers view, or with Ollama only (zero cloud keys).
#   Do NOT set PORT or DISABLE_HMR there — they are local-dev only.
#   Full deployment steps: README -> "Deploying to Vercel".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
